{"raw": {"https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1335054": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Math", "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Math. Mount Mercy University. St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University | Adjunct Instructor - Math St. Ambrose University and Mount Mercy University invite applications for an adjunct faculty pool to teach undergraduate mathematics, statistics, and related courses at our Davenport and Cedar Rapids, Iowa campuses. We are seeking qualified professionals and educators interested in teaching during Spring 2027 and future fall, spring, and summer semesters. Applicants with expertise in mathematics, statistics, applied mathematics, data science, or related fields are encouraged to apply. All positions require in-person instruction. Candidates may indicate their availability for one or both campuses and the courses they are qualified and interested in teaching. Current Spring 2027 Teaching Opportunities Mount Mercy University, Cedar Rapids, Iowa MATH-171: Elementary Functions Additional teaching opportunities at either university may become available based on enrollment, scheduling, and departmental needs. Mathematics Adjunct Pool In addition to the current vacancies, we welcome applications from candidates qualified to teach courses in the following areas: Introductory and college-level mathematics College algebra and precalculus Calculus and differential equations Probability and statistics Linear algebra and discrete mathematics Applied mathematics Data science and related quantitative disciplines Applicants do not need to be qualified or available to teach every subject listed. Course assignments will depend on institutional needs and individual qualifications. Qualifications A master's degree or higher in mathematics, statistics, applied mathematics, data science, or a closely related discipline is preferred. Candidates with appropriate graduate-level academic preparation in the subject they would teach are also encouraged to apply. Previous college-level teaching experience is preferred but not required. Relevant professional experience and demonstrated subject-matter expertise will also be considered. Applicants must be available to teach in person at the St. Ambrose University campus in Davenport, Iowa, or the Mount Mercy University campus in Cedar Rapids, Iowa. Application Interested applicants should submit a current curriculum vitae or r\u00e9sum\u00e9 and a brief cover letter describing their academic background, relevant professional or teaching experience, and areas of instructional expertise. Applicants should indicate their preferred campus or campuses, the courses or subject areas they are qualified to teach, and their availability for Spring 2027 or future semesters. Applications will be reviewed as teaching needs arise. Inclusion in the adjunct faculty pool does not guarantee a teaching assignment. Our Mission St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses, including Mount Mercy University, are an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners. Together, we empower all members of our community to act courageously, seek wisdom through faith and reason, work for justice and mercy, and lead lives of service. St. Ambrose University and its affiliated institutions are equal opportunity employers. #HEJ"}, "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1327232": {"title": "Public Safety Officer", "description": "Public Safety Officer. Mount Mercy University. Public Safety Officer Mount Mercy University is seeking a dedicated and service-oriented Public Safety Officer to join our Public Safety team. This position plays a vital role in maintaining a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Public Safety Officers work a non-standard schedule and assist in providing 24/7 campus safety coverage. This position would cover hours from 4 PM to Midnight, Saturday through Wednesday. The starting pay is $16.50 an hour. The ideal candidate is a collaborative professional who demonstrates sound judgment, strong interpersonal skills, and a commitment to serving a diverse university community. Key Responsibilities Patrol campus buildings, parking lots, and grounds to help ensure the safety and security of people and property. Enforce campus security and parking policies, including building access and key control procedures. Respond to emergencies, provide assistance to injured individuals, and coordinate with local emergency responders when necessary. Conduct investigations, complete incident reports, and maintain security records. Monitor security and life-safety systems, including fire, intrusion, and access control systems. Perform routine inspections of campus safety equipment and security measures. Provide security escorts, support campus events, and collaborate with departments on safety initiatives and emergency preparedness. Participate in safety training, emergency drills, and other professional development activities. Deliver excellent customer service while maintaining a visible, approachable presence on campus. Qualifications Required High school diploma or equivalent. Valid driver's license. First Aid and CPR certification (or ability to obtain upon hire). Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and other non-traditional hours as needed. Preferred Associate degree. Previous experience in campus safety, security, law enforcement, military service, emergency response, or related field. Desired Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Commitment to the mission and values of a faith-based university. Strong communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills. Ability to exercise sound judgment, de-escalate conflicts, and respond effectively in emergencies. Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to maintain confidentiality. Proficiency with technology and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively. Benefits Competitive salary commensurate with experience. Comprehensive benefits package, including medical, dental, vision, and retirement plans. Generous paid time off and holidays. Tuition Remission. Professional development opportunities. Supportive and collaborative work environment. Access to campus amenities, cultural events, and recreational facilities. St. Ambrose University and its affiliate campuses, including Mount Mercy University in Cedar Rapids, Iowa, are an inclusive, Catholic, and diocesan community of learners. Together, we empower all members of our community to act courageously, to seek wisdom through faith and reason, to work for justice and mercy, and to lead lives of service. St. Ambrose University and its affiliated institutions within its Catholic higher education network are equal opportunity employers. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit your resume, cover letter, and contact information for three professional references through our online application portal at https://stambroseuniv.applicantlist.com . Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the position is filled. St. Ambrose is an equal opportunity employer. #HEJ"}}, "rows": {"https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1335054": {"school_id": 332, "posting_url": "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1335054", "job_title_in_post": "Adjunct Instructor - Math", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Math; Introductory", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1327232": {"school_id": 332, "posting_url": "https://mtmercy.applicantlist.com/jobs/1327232", "job_title_in_post": "Public Safety Officer", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 332, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:40:42+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:40:42+00:00", "last_error": ""}